---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import {
  ToolbarStatusOutcomes,
  ToolbarStatusPlayground,
  ToolbarStatusSelection,
} from '../../components/ToolbarStatusDemo';
---

<Docs
  title="Toolbar Status"
  description="A compact toolbar button that reports what an action did and opens the details."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Toolbar Status</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A small button that takes the place of an action once it finishes. It says what happened in a word or two, announces
    the full message, and opens a popover with the details and a follow-up action.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <ToolbarStatusPlayground client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Toolbar status usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import { ToolbarStatus } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/toolbar-status";

const failed = note.startsWith("Export failed");

<ToolbarStatus
  label={failed ? "Export failed" : "Export result"}
  message={note}
  error={failed}
>
  <Button variant="outline" size="sm" disabled={busy} onClick={run}>
    {failed ? "Retry export" : "Export again"}
  </Button>
</ToolbarStatus>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>label</code> is the button text and the popover title. Keep it to two words so it fits a narrow slot; longer
      labels end in an ellipsis. <code>message</code> is the full explanation. It shows in the popover and screen
      readers hear it as soon as it changes.
    </p>
    <p>
      Set <code>error</code> for a failure. The button turns destructive, the title turns red, and the message is
      announced with <code>role="alert"</code>. Otherwise the button is outline and the message uses{' '}
      <code>role="status"</code>. The button is always the small size.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>children</code> sit under the message, usually one small outline button to run the action again. Pass
      nothing for a message-only status. <code>defaultOpen</code> opens the details once when the status mounts. The
      popover aligns to the end of the button.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Outcomes</h2>
    <p>
      Success, capped, cancelled, and failed exports, a busy table that disables the follow-up, a message-only save, and
      a failed save that opens on mount.
    </p>
    <ToolbarStatusOutcomes client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section" id="toolbar-status-selection">
    <h2 class="section-title">Selected rows</h2>
    <p>
      In a bulk action bar the status replaces <em>Export selected</em> after the export. On a narrow bar the other
      actions move into an <em>Actions</em> menu. Selection, export, and delete in these examples are sample code. The
      package only draws the status.
    </p>
    <ToolbarStatusSelection client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The live message sits outside the popover, so it is announced even while the popover is closed. The button opens
      with <kbd>Enter</kbd> or <kbd>Space</kbd>, <kbd>Tab</kbd> moves into the action, and <kbd>Escape</kbd> closes the
      popover and returns focus to the button. The popover fades in over 120ms; reduced motion turns it off.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
